    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compĕdĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conp-</span></b> ), no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ĭtum,
			4, v. a.
			compes, <i>to fetter</i>, <i>shackle</i> (mostly anteand post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: pedes corrigiis, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 28, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servi conpediti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 56</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 5, 1, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Tranq. 10, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 4, 3, 7, § 7
			al.</span></i>—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rebus immortalibus perniciosissime compediri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 39</span></i>
			.</div>
